// The shortcuts of the `interface` example (docs/adr/0142-input-and-focus.md): each `scope` is
// `global` or the class of an element that holds the focus, and each of its children a chord of the
// keys' meaning, which names a command that the example does; `Primary` is Ctrl, or ⌘ on macOS.

scope global {
    T switch-theme
    Primary+O open
}
